  "name": "Pokémon Snap Photo Contest (64 Mario Stadium)",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "In 1999 Nintendo's TV show 64 Mario Stadium and CoroCoro Comic each ran a Best Photo Contest for Pokémon Snap, which came out on the Nintendo 64 in Japan on 21 March 1999. Players printed their photos as stickers and mailed them in on a postcard, and five winners from each contest had their photo made into a card, credited \"Photo.\" where a card names its illustrator, with a bottom edge naming it a \"Best Photo Contest\" prize card. 64 Mario Stadium's five were Articuno, Chansey, Charmander, Koffing and Squirtle. Each winner got 15 copies of their card, against 20 for CoroCoro's, after lending Nintendo the game cartridge that held the photo's save data. A few other copies have been sold by Yuichi Konno, one of the card game's original developers, probably spares from the print run.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: 1999 Pokemon Snap Photo Contests",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/1999-pokemon-snap-photo-contests/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Johto Times: Interview with Tsukasa Hosono",
        "url": "https://johto.substack.com/p/interview-with-tsukasa-hosono-english"
      }
    ]
  },
